"""Real headlines for the Chainlink, Stellar and rank 11-20 entity rules
(config/entities.yaml).

Every case is a published headline, some with the first sentence or the feed
excerpt, collected on 2026-10-01 (KST; 2026-09-30 in UTC) with its source URL,
the publication date as found (or why it could not be checked) and a short
note: the institution for positives, the collision for negatives. "The
previous rule" in a note means the rules of commit 93881dd, which these
replaced. The headlines are short quotes kept to test the matcher; article
text is not copied. Figures in them are quotes, not market data (market
figures belong in research/). No title from stellar.org's own blog is used,
because its terms forbid public reuse; third-party coverage of the same news
is used instead.

" || " marks where a title ends and its excerpt starts. The pipeline joins
title and excerpt with a space (collector/pipeline.py), and so does this test.

GOLD holds the headlines collected for each entity. VERIFY holds headlines from
an independent check that earlier drafts of the rules missed ("pos") or wrongly
matched ("neg"); they are kept as regression cases. Synthetic red-team
headlines, and the trade-offs accepted for recall, are in
tests/test_entities_ranks_11_20.py.
"""

